WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.323
Look at one computer, sitting on its
own. It cannot send anything anywhere.

2
00:00:09.543 --> 00:00:12.747
Join it to another, and
the two of them can share.

3
00:00:13.247 --> 00:00:15.337
Here is one computer, on its own.

4
00:00:15.557 --> 00:00:17.832
It cannot send anything anywhere.

5
00:00:18.052 --> 00:00:21.210
Now take a cable, and join
it to another computer.

6
00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:24.867
Straight away they can send each
other messages and pictures.

7
00:00:25.087 --> 00:00:29.220
Devices joined together so they
can share are called a network.

8
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:33.621
At home, every device joins
the network through one box.

9
00:00:33.841 --> 00:00:37.231
It is called a router, and it
has little blinking lights.

10
00:00:37.451 --> 00:00:40.748
The laptop and the printer
plug into it with a wire.

11
00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:44.219
The tablet and the phone
join with no wire at all.

12
00:00:44.439 --> 00:00:48.665
Now the tablet can send a picture
to the printer, through the router.

13
00:00:49.165 --> 00:00:52.741
A wired device has a cable
carrying its connection.

14
00:00:52.961 --> 00:00:58.394
A desktop computer with a cable into
the wall is wired. So are headphones.

15
00:00:58.614 --> 00:01:02.794
A wireless device connects through
the air, with no cable at all.

16
00:01:03.014 --> 00:01:07.333
A tablet is wireless. So is a
phone, and so is a smart watch.

17
00:01:07.553 --> 00:01:11.640
Both are connected. You just
cannot see the wireless one.

18
00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:15.390
Your home network is one of
millions, all around the world.

19
00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:19.279
Join all of those networks
together, and you have the internet.

20
00:01:19.499 --> 00:01:21.775
Your home joins it through the router.

21
00:01:21.995 --> 00:01:25.803
So does a school far away.
So does Grandma's phone.

22
00:01:26.023 --> 00:01:30.156
Send Grandma a message, and it crosses
the whole world in about a second.

23
00:01:30.376 --> 00:01:35.159
The internet is not one big computer.
It is millions of them, joined.

24
00:01:35.659 --> 00:01:38.678
Sometimes the internet
is not available at all.

25
00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:42.845
On a plane, in a tunnel, or
when the router at home breaks.

26
00:01:43.065 --> 00:01:46.130
Switch it off, and try
each thing on the tablet.

27
00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:51.923
A video online stops. A video
call stops. A message cannot go.

28
00:01:52.143 --> 00:01:55.673
All three need other computers,
and they cannot be reached.

29
00:01:55.893 --> 00:02:00.397
Drawing still works. A saved game
still works. Your photos still work.

30
00:02:00.617 --> 00:02:03.868
They are already on the tablet,
so they need nobody else.

31
00:02:04.368 --> 00:02:07.990
A network is devices joined
together so they can share.

32
00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:12.622
At home they join through the router,
some with a wire and some with none.

33
00:02:12.842 --> 00:02:16.836
The internet is many computers
joined together around the world.

34
00:02:17.056 --> 00:02:22.164
And there are times when it is not
there. Then everything else carries on.
